      "Language": "por",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 30 years old, male, patient with rare multiple aneurysms of sinus of Valsalva associated to mitral and aortic regurgitation and total occlusion of circumflex artery had the clinical diagnosis made accidentally. The multiple aneurysms were detected by transesophageal echodopplercardiography and hemodynamic study. The diagnosis were confirmed at surgery and the patient underwent correction of the aneurysms through the use of pericardial patches and mitral and aortic valve replacement."},
